1
00:00:00,559 --> 00:00:02,390
You've seen these videos.

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:04,929
Minecraft, but the floor is lava.

3
00:00:05,419 --> 00:00:07,040
Minecraft, but every chunk is made

4
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:08,750
of one random block.

5
00:00:09,259 --> 00:00:11,300
Minecraft, but if you move on a red light,

6
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:14,541
you die. They look like the most fun

7
00:00:14,541 --> 00:00:17,051
anyone has ever had in this game.

8
00:00:17,361 --> 00:00:18,741
And for a long time,

9
00:00:18,741 --> 00:00:20,261
the only way to play them was

10
00:00:20,261 --> 00:00:22,291
to watch somebody else do it.

11
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:26,160
Not anymore. This is Challenge Craft,

12
00:00:26,160 --> 00:00:27,580
a free mod that puts fifty

13
00:00:27,580 --> 00:00:30,100
of those challenges into your own world,

14
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:32,990
ready to play, alone or with your friends.

15
00:00:34,348 --> 00:00:35,958
Here's how it works.

16
00:00:36,248 --> 00:00:37,728
When you create a new world,

17
00:00:37,728 --> 00:00:39,698
there's a new tab called Challenges.

18
00:00:40,128 --> 00:00:41,508
Every challenge is a card,

19
00:00:41,508 --> 00:00:42,928
and you can pick just one,

20
00:00:42,928 --> 00:00:45,378
or stack as many as you dare.

21
00:00:46,190 --> 00:00:47,750
Every combination gets

22
00:00:47,750 --> 00:00:48,650
a difficulty rating,

23
00:00:48,650 --> 00:00:51,520
and that rating decides your reward.

24
00:00:51,850 --> 00:00:53,900
A gentle twist pays a little.

25
00:00:54,050 --> 00:00:56,740
A truly brutal combination pays a lot.

26
00:00:57,523 --> 00:01:00,083
Then you play. The goal is the same

27
00:01:00,083 --> 00:01:02,913
as always: beat the Ender Dragon.

28
00:01:03,143 --> 00:01:04,703
A timer tracks your run,

29
00:01:04,703 --> 00:01:06,123
and every challenge shows you

30
00:01:06,123 --> 00:01:08,453
on screen exactly what it's doing.

31
00:01:09,254 --> 00:01:10,964
When the dragon falls,

32
00:01:11,174 --> 00:01:13,624
you get a run summary card with your time,

33
00:01:13,834 --> 00:01:15,354
your difficulty and your XP.

34
00:01:15,354 --> 00:01:17,094
You can save it as an image

35
00:01:17,094 --> 00:01:19,024
and share it right away.

36
00:01:20,309 --> 00:01:22,939
And that XP is the clever part.

37
00:01:23,209 --> 00:01:24,749
It's Lifetime XP,

38
00:01:24,749 --> 00:01:26,859
which means it never goes away.

39
00:01:27,069 --> 00:01:29,029
It carries over into every new world

40
00:01:29,029 --> 00:01:31,219
and every server you play on.

41
00:01:31,937 --> 00:01:34,557
Lifetime XP fills a level tree

42
00:01:34,557 --> 00:01:36,147
from one to twenty.

43
00:01:36,497 --> 00:01:38,157
Every level unlocks new challenges,

44
00:01:38,157 --> 00:01:40,197
so you start with a handful

45
00:01:40,197 --> 00:01:44,068
and slowly work your way up to all fifty.

46
00:01:44,068 --> 00:01:47,008
Levels also unlock permanent perks,

47
00:01:47,008 --> 00:01:48,288
like night vision,

48
00:01:48,288 --> 00:01:50,408
extra hearts or extra strength,

49
00:01:50,408 --> 00:01:52,738
for every run you start from then on.

50
00:01:53,068 --> 00:01:54,688
And past level twenty,

51
00:01:54,688 --> 00:01:56,628
you collect Infinity Stars,

52
00:01:56,628 --> 00:01:58,408
which give your name a colored aura

53
00:01:58,408 --> 00:02:00,958
that everyone on the server can see.

54
00:02:02,122 --> 00:02:04,332
So what can you actually play?

55
00:02:04,602 --> 00:02:05,522
Let's take a look at some

56
00:02:05,522 --> 00:02:07,502
of the challenges, because this is

57
00:02:07,502 --> 00:02:09,432
where the mod really shines.

58
00:02:10,893 --> 00:02:11,793
Red Light,

59
00:02:11,793 --> 00:02:13,613
Green Light turns the whole world

60
00:02:13,613 --> 00:02:15,103
into the famous game.

61
00:02:15,453 --> 00:02:17,473
While the light is green, you can run,

62
00:02:17,473 --> 00:02:19,893
mine and fight. When it turns yellow,

63
00:02:19,893 --> 00:02:21,483
you have three seconds.

64
00:02:21,713 --> 00:02:24,083
And on red, nothing is allowed to move.

65
00:02:24,313 --> 00:02:25,753
Not a step, not a jump,

66
00:02:25,753 --> 00:02:27,163
not even your camera.

67
00:02:28,001 --> 00:02:30,761
In Dice Movement, you throw a real die

68
00:02:30,761 --> 00:02:32,851
that tumbles across the ground.

69
00:02:33,201 --> 00:02:35,301
However many pips land face up,

70
00:02:35,301 --> 00:02:37,381
that's how many blocks you may walk,

71
00:02:37,381 --> 00:02:38,561
and a ring around you shows

72
00:02:38,561 --> 00:02:40,531
how far you can still go.

73
00:02:41,359 --> 00:02:42,939
And in Cushion Only,

74
00:02:42,939 --> 00:02:44,349
you can't walk at all.

75
00:02:44,619 --> 00:02:46,639
You place a cushion, you sit on it,

76
00:02:46,639 --> 00:02:48,429
and you stand up where it was.

77
00:02:48,639 --> 00:02:50,019
Every journey becomes a chain

78
00:02:50,019 --> 00:02:51,289
of little hops.

79
00:02:52,606 --> 00:02:55,516
Some challenges change the world itself.

80
00:02:55,986 --> 00:02:57,486
With Random Chunk Blocks,

81
00:02:57,486 --> 00:02:59,106
every single chunk is rebuilt

82
00:02:59,106 --> 00:03:01,076
from one random block.

83
00:03:01,406 --> 00:03:03,586
One step you're walking on gold,

84
00:03:03,586 --> 00:03:05,166
the next on redstone,

85
00:03:05,166 --> 00:03:05,586
and the next

86
00:03:05,586 --> 00:03:07,696
on something completely different.

87
00:03:08,434 --> 00:03:09,994
Skyblock drops you

88
00:03:09,994 --> 00:03:11,594
on a tiny island in the void.

89
00:03:11,594 --> 00:03:13,844
And in The Floor is Lava,

90
00:03:14,034 --> 00:03:16,054
you start burning the moment you stand still

91
00:03:16,054 --> 00:03:17,014
for three seconds,

92
00:03:17,014 --> 00:03:20,144
or the moment you touch natural ground.

93
00:03:21,085 --> 00:03:23,175
Chunk Hunt is even stranger.

94
00:03:23,705 --> 00:03:25,755
Every time you enter a new chunk,

95
00:03:25,985 --> 00:03:27,705
the border locks around you,

96
00:03:27,705 --> 00:03:29,245
and you have to defeat a glowing

97
00:03:29,245 --> 00:03:31,995
target mob before you're allowed to leave.

98
00:03:33,241 --> 00:03:35,291
Then there are the mob challenges.

99
00:03:35,881 --> 00:03:36,921
In Size Matters,

100
00:03:36,921 --> 00:03:39,551
every mob spawns at a random size.

101
00:03:40,041 --> 00:03:41,441
Tiny ones are fast,

102
00:03:41,441 --> 00:03:42,861
and giant ones have more health

103
00:03:42,861 --> 00:03:44,331
and a longer reach.

104
00:03:44,661 --> 00:03:47,301
And Double Trouble multiplies every spawn,

105
00:03:47,301 --> 00:03:48,811
up to ten times.

106
00:03:49,121 --> 00:03:51,671
One zombie is never just one zombie.

107
00:03:52,542 --> 00:03:54,672
Drops get the same treatment.

108
00:03:55,022 --> 00:03:56,702
With Upside Down Drops,

109
00:03:56,702 --> 00:03:58,222
everything you break floats up

110
00:03:58,222 --> 00:03:58,762
into the sky,

111
00:03:58,762 --> 00:04:01,232
so you'd better catch it fast.

112
00:04:01,622 --> 00:04:03,302
Random Block Drops makes every

113
00:04:03,302 --> 00:04:06,042
block drop something completely different,

114
00:04:06,042 --> 00:04:08,562
and Progressive Block Drops only unlocks a block

115
00:04:08,562 --> 00:04:10,212
once you've mined the target shown

116
00:04:10,212 --> 00:04:14,349
on your screen. And some challenges are

117
00:04:14,349 --> 00:04:17,989
complete game modes. In Force Item Battle,

118
00:04:17,989 --> 00:04:19,149
every player gets their

119
00:04:19,149 --> 00:04:21,209
own random target item,

120
00:04:21,209 --> 00:04:23,159
floating right above their head.

121
00:04:23,449 --> 00:04:25,509
Whoever collects the most items before

122
00:04:25,509 --> 00:04:27,499
the timer runs out wins.

123
00:04:28,505 --> 00:04:30,845
Lockout Bingo puts up to four teams

124
00:04:30,845 --> 00:04:33,675
on one shared five by five board.

125
00:04:34,065 --> 00:04:36,405
Every goal can only be claimed once,

126
00:04:36,405 --> 00:04:38,005
so every tile you take is

127
00:04:38,005 --> 00:04:40,555
a tile your rivals will never get.

128
00:04:41,296 --> 00:04:43,426
There's also All Biomes,

129
00:04:43,616 --> 00:04:44,276
where the whole server

130
00:04:44,276 --> 00:04:47,356
shares one checklist, Minecraft Trivia,

131
00:04:47,356 --> 00:04:49,436
where you answer a question every two minutes

132
00:04:49,436 --> 00:04:51,796
or die, and the ultimate grinds,

133
00:04:51,796 --> 00:04:53,946
All Items and All Entities.

134
00:04:55,364 --> 00:04:56,724
But the challenge everyone

135
00:04:56,724 --> 00:04:58,944
talks about is number fifty,

136
00:04:58,944 --> 00:05:00,634
The House Always Wins.

137
00:05:01,004 --> 00:05:02,444
It turns your survival world

138
00:05:02,444 --> 00:05:06,186
into a casino. Every item you own

139
00:05:06,186 --> 00:05:08,396
is suddenly worth casino chips.

140
00:05:08,746 --> 00:05:09,026
You cash

141
00:05:09,026 --> 00:05:10,686
in at the dealer's booth at spawn,

142
00:05:10,686 --> 00:05:13,096
and he will happily buy your loot.

143
00:05:13,366 --> 00:05:14,606
But every ten minutes,

144
00:05:14,606 --> 00:05:15,806
the House collects a fee

145
00:05:15,806 --> 00:05:16,686
from the whole team,

146
00:05:16,686 --> 00:05:18,796
and that fee keeps climbing.

147
00:05:19,186 --> 00:05:20,846
If you can't pay, the House wins,

148
00:05:20,846 --> 00:05:22,796
and your run is over.

149
00:05:23,579 --> 00:05:25,759
So you can farm the money the slow way,

150
00:05:25,759 --> 00:05:27,119
or you can gamble.

151
00:05:27,119 --> 00:05:31,139
Mine Fever is a five reel slot machine with free spins

152
00:05:31,139 --> 00:05:32,379
and a top prize

153
00:05:32,379 --> 00:05:34,789
of five thousand times your bet.

154
00:05:35,059 --> 00:05:36,839
You can even bet a whole stack of items,

155
00:05:36,839 --> 00:05:39,069
and win it back as a fountain.

156
00:05:39,908 --> 00:05:42,048
There's Plinko, where you drop the ball

157
00:05:42,048 --> 00:05:43,618
and pray for the edges.

158
00:05:43,928 --> 00:05:45,888
There's Crash, where a rocket climbs

159
00:05:45,888 --> 00:05:47,408
and the multiplier grows,

160
00:05:47,408 --> 00:05:50,198
until you cash out, or it explodes.

161
00:05:50,608 --> 00:05:52,088
And there's a full roulette table,

162
00:05:52,088 --> 00:05:53,948
where you place your chips right

163
00:05:53,948 --> 00:05:56,829
on the felt. Of course,

164
00:05:56,829 --> 00:05:59,019
the House always wins in the end.

165
00:05:59,349 --> 00:06:01,689
Every game pays back ninety six percent

166
00:06:01,689 --> 00:06:03,549
on average, and every lost bet

167
00:06:03,549 --> 00:06:05,829
sends monsters after you.

168
00:06:05,829 --> 00:06:08,719
The bigger the loss, the nastier the wave.

169
00:06:09,612 --> 00:06:10,992
And if you die?

170
00:06:10,992 --> 00:06:12,492
You lose a quarter of your chips,

171
00:06:12,492 --> 00:06:14,112
and the dealer deals you a hand

172
00:06:14,112 --> 00:06:16,132
of Blackjack. Win,

173
00:06:16,132 --> 00:06:17,732
and you stand up right where you fell,

174
00:06:17,732 --> 00:06:19,482
with everything you had.

175
00:06:19,672 --> 00:06:21,762
Lose, and you're dead for real.

176
00:06:23,042 --> 00:06:24,742
Every single challenge works

177
00:06:24,742 --> 00:06:25,772
in multiplayer.

178
00:06:26,602 --> 00:06:28,702
Levels and XP sync to every player,

179
00:06:28,702 --> 00:06:31,402
and name tags show everyone's level

180
00:06:31,402 --> 00:06:32,332
and aura.

181
00:06:33,195 --> 00:06:35,015
You can save your favorite setups

182
00:06:35,015 --> 00:06:37,415
as presets, or turn any run

183
00:06:37,415 --> 00:06:38,895
into a short challenge code,

184
00:06:38,895 --> 00:06:41,735
seed included. Send it to a friend,

185
00:06:41,735 --> 00:06:44,235
and they play the exact same world

186
00:06:44,235 --> 00:06:45,815
with the exact same rules.

187
00:06:45,815 --> 00:06:48,615
And every day there's a Daily Challenge,

188
00:06:48,615 --> 00:06:51,415
one ruleset and one seed for everyone,

189
00:06:51,415 --> 00:06:53,135
so you can come back tomorrow

190
00:06:53,135 --> 00:06:54,985
and beat your best time.

191
00:06:56,178 --> 00:06:58,188
And if nobody's online?

192
00:06:58,438 --> 00:06:59,558
Open the Lockout lobby

193
00:06:59,558 --> 00:07:01,228
and play against Bob.

194
00:07:01,558 --> 00:07:03,378
Bob is an AI player who

195
00:07:03,378 --> 00:07:05,518
plays the board just like you do.

196
00:07:05,518 --> 00:07:08,818
He reads the goals, plans a route, mines,

197
00:07:08,818 --> 00:07:10,018
crafts, fights,

198
00:07:10,018 --> 00:07:11,518
and even builds a Nether portal

199
00:07:11,518 --> 00:07:12,988
to claim his tiles.

200
00:07:13,970 --> 00:07:15,030
Bob is still

201
00:07:15,030 --> 00:07:17,310
in an early stage of development,

202
00:07:17,310 --> 00:07:18,930
so he makes mistakes,

203
00:07:18,930 --> 00:07:20,150
and sometimes he dies

204
00:07:20,150 --> 00:07:22,120
in very creative ways.

205
00:07:22,470 --> 00:07:23,610
But he learns new tricks

206
00:07:23,610 --> 00:07:27,459
with every update. So whether you want

207
00:07:27,459 --> 00:07:29,869
to play your favorite YouTube challenge,

208
00:07:30,159 --> 00:07:31,409
race your friends,

209
00:07:31,579 --> 00:07:33,299
or find out how long you can survive

210
00:07:33,299 --> 00:07:34,859
against the House,

211
00:07:34,859 --> 00:07:36,889
there's a run waiting for you.

212
00:07:37,601 --> 00:07:39,821
Challenge Craft is completely free

213
00:07:39,821 --> 00:07:41,171
on CurseForge.

214
00:07:41,501 --> 00:07:43,031
The link is in the description.

215
00:07:43,421 --> 00:07:45,301
Pick a challenge, invite your friends,

216
00:07:45,301 --> 00:07:47,371
and see how far you can get.

